WEBVTT

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.127
Two thousand years ago,

00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:05.140
the founding text of
Chinese medicine opens

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:05.702
on a boast —

00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:07.950
and the emperor himself is
the one who makes it.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.762
I have heard that the
people of high antiquity all

00:00:13.762 --> 00:00:14.956
lived past a hundred years.

00:00:14.956 --> 00:00:16.327
Their movements never
weakened.

00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:18.317
The years did not wear
them down as they wear

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:18.450
us.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.300
It's false. Not exaggerated
— false.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.261
They did not.

00:00:32.261 --> 00:00:34.288
The people who wrote that
sentence died younger

00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:35.927
than the ancestors they
were praising.

00:00:35.927 --> 00:00:37.653
The golden age was
already a memory that

00:00:37.653 --> 00:00:38.300
never happened.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.490
So why did an entire
civilisation copy that one

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.874
sentence, faithfully, for
two thousand years?

00:00:45.874 --> 00:00:47.993
The Emperor's Inner
Canon. Chapter One —

00:00:47.993 --> 00:00:49.000
The First Sentence.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.877
A dramatized adaptation of
a classical philosophical

00:00:55.877 --> 00:00:57.500
text. Not medical advice.
